{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_215c76b1af08b84eb4f57767c371bd3a8d8337a0e04422881bd9b067122752d4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"brutusin/instrumentation@f1c80c2524a1 snapshot eba29e281a7e6777","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b59f32442b0fcf7b3dfc308bada39b65c7afed67b95ba6ca6c8d56fdfa75271a","slc_f93c3ad75351275157580ce8e0712369ed512da34ac1c309e313f4195031267f"],"source_ids":["src_db91aa82fec6527ca5f319f8cd834734"],"text":"Transformed methods are wrapped so an onStart call precedes the body, onFinished fires on normal return, and onThrowable is invoked and the throwable rethrown on error.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_24528ca1bdda2761bf77f8f736dfae4976235a918d8b3f6a0a922a980b8a7e55","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"brutusin/instrumentation@f1c80c2524a1 snapshot eba29e281a7e6777","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_81aa10281b34fa8d7b64588d9234b4689e1388b6af228e57bd7baf54d28a3a93"],"source_ids":["src_db91aa82fec6527ca5f319f8cd834734"],"text":"The framework uses the ASM library to inject instructions into method definitions of classes being loaded.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3f3c0196ac00caaf31ca4a6cf2d35758960c83cc9cfe2d467427384904aab5f7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"brutusin/instrumentation@f1c80c2524a1 snapshot eba29e281a7e6777","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_43470636aa8ac9522d3456870a46546202372208ddb3cd31503422013e82d475","slc_468aa363b6f521cb2c35cf49d6b07d71d26cdf5b6a1939b215e239f26156df12","slc_59e9c28ea639234863c660189c434e473954c5639961cf0a14861a15872cb360","slc_69d3b31cc64665267a3ae8f2c48bc6272e2dc4b03a30219cd5822ab106bf906e","slc_a7d9b482799b31f85947c71e5274c9ab6ca2e15988184338e2696869eb248769","slc_ce10d0dc77230df26a548f07a2f77011852755c8566e161eaeed3f2c74e93110"],"source_ids":["src_db91aa82fec6527ca5f319f8cd834734"],"text":"Custom interceptors can filter targets via interceptClass(className, byteCode) and interceptMethod(ClassNode, MethodNode) hooks, and implement lifecycle callbacks including doOnStart, doOnFinish, doOnThrowableThrown, and doOnThrowableUncatched, each receiving the Method, relevant payload, and an executionId.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3f62c514c38311429a2087520347796b77c341624049f3dd7391005a4cf8db5a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"brutusin/instrumentation@f1c80c2524a1 snapshot eba29e281a7e6777","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ffee9e928120102c5a2d351561260ded87ebc9e1884e2a3281f772e2b7372207"],"source_ids":["src_db91aa82fec6527ca5f319f8cd834734"],"text":"The project is an extensible Java agent framework that instruments JVM programs by modifying bytecode at class-loading time to capture method invocation events (start, finish, errors) and notify custom listeners.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4448072f61d662e9e2e674571d9a8ac371ea9f1db92f7526ffd653d3bd96a9e7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"brutusin/instrumentation@f1c80c2524a1 snapshot eba29e281a7e6777","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_06425205f4628e3261a4750c6158c7017cf0ec0895c4beb7c0c2f3c9839695c5","slc_394fc0eec175f6e25197abc56a99f234f3b07ba3965b21647dcd2628c3ace4d9","slc_c4cec85a6c682e99a73bbb6e01848cef7a2651a67f604b1879d9cdb4d96a1fe8"],"source_ids":["src_db91aa82fec6527ca5f319f8cd834734"],"text":"The project is licensed under Apache License, Version 2.0, authored by Ignacio del Valle Alles, with support and bug reports handled through the GitHub issues page.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a229bb0d40bcf0d851ac39bc427c686b964d71a993dd376c40a1a034346eafdd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"brutusin/instrumentation@f1c80c2524a1 snapshot eba29e281a7e6777","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_23a18c6c4e9f7403eb1acf233940716648704335cc9e60b2d0bb670f688fd631","slc_6c1a98d8bb655fb64fb7603cd34cc019bbc9532cdf3e2ce9b8cb320789bb1718"],"source_ids":["src_db91aa82fec6527ca5f319f8cd834734"],"text":"Deployment workflow: build a fat-jar containing the interceptor class, add 'Premain-Class: org.brutusin.instrumentation.Agent' to the manifest, and launch the target application with -javaagent:myagent.jar=InterceptorClass;optional_parameter on at least JRE 1.5.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a3541efc1d76c3cd4ce15bf5b9204c9a5e02648e2715854e4d212c8f3c0bd2a2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"brutusin/instrumentation@f1c80c2524a1 snapshot eba29e281a7e6777","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_23a18c6c4e9f7403eb1acf233940716648704335cc9e60b2d0bb670f688fd631","slc_99c3b4b662b1c09b52f394a18b7ff6e5aec575b9e2d8eb6b350256f764380b2b"],"source_ids":["src_db91aa82fec6527ca5f319f8cd834734"],"text":"Interceptors receive an init(String arg) callback with an optional parameter supplied through the JVM agent arguments.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a6bc451443aff029121ce9edb2b0953c9fd3febe76291cbbf1ea39173998c752","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"brutusin/instrumentation@f1c80c2524a1 snapshot eba29e281a7e6777","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0df552c1b8a835db607d5fdffe69f0a0a302378e3044f535b58e7350db54e07d","slc_fb263cc09e7bc7275943c08e5059414200b7b7e3b0619d70ba6f7d9cc9c172c8"],"source_ids":["src_db91aa82fec6527ca5f319f8cd834734"],"text":"A complete working example is available in the separate brutusin/logging-instrumentation repository, which is listed as a dependent module.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","created_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ab3743db6e359fa943a0a4a1327cea80abf7a3c56154611856997284a59707f1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"brutusin/instrumentation@f1c80c2524a1 snapshot eba29e281a7e6777","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_50551d3c73bb0636a9a7d143f64721609430ec2f73a2d1856af04c6ec34c58e5"],"source_ids":["src_db91aa82fec6527ca5f319f8cd834734"],"text":"Instrumentation is implemented as a byte[]-to-byte[] class transformation at load time, leveraging the JDK 1.5 java.lang.instrument package's java-agent mechanism.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:37Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9631b75ec3e8427ba72d1da73a6e8a89"}
